{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1398722-mundane-implants-wired-and-prerequisites-for-other-merits","id":1398722,"title":"Mundane Implants: Wired and Prerequisites For Other Merits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-24T23:41:30-07:00","id":1398722,"title":"Mundane Implants: Wired and Prerequisites For Other Merits","content":"I have a character that uses Mundane Implants in a different game and was wondering how the +1 die to an Attribute relates to prerequisites for other merits. For example, lets say you bought Wired: Dexterity on your normal Dexterity 2. Now you want Fighting Finesse, which requires Dexterity 3. Does Wired allow you to circumvent the requisite? RAW I would say no, but what about RAI or on your own table?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Things need not have happened to be true. Tales and dreams are the shadow truths that will endure when mere facts are dust and ashes, and forgot.&quot; Sandman (Neil Gaiman)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/733-troller","name":"Troller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar733_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T05:21:42-07:00","id":1398756,"title":"","content":"Dave Brookshaw (at the time lead dev for Mage, but the same should totally be applicable for Demon) stated that he'd be totally okay with players boosting their stats to fulfil Merit prerequisites with spells, but that they'd lose access to those Merits the moment the spell ends.<br /> <br /> Quick edit: Wired states that the +1 bonus applies to rolls. I don't think that would be specified if they intended for it to apply for anything other than rolls. Unlike the mage spell example, you don't get an extra dot, only a +1 modifier. (That also means you don't increase derived stats like Speed or Defense.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 06-25-2020, 08:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}